+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of seconds,
+like `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups, like `1h30m`. The units
+are `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may
+appear at most once, in that order, without spaces. Units are case-insensitive,
+so `45S` is the same as `45s`. Negative and decimal values are not accepted. A
+`timedelta` default is passed through unchanged.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait)
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1h30m"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=90"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=30m1h"])
+```
+
